e to see now that  people are coming  back out to associate with each other  it's made and built in a way that people  can interact with each other madison  kimbrough 8 news now  there will be several more meetings  before the park does reopen and that is  scheduled to reopen in 2023  and not far from huntred circle park  there is of course the huntridge theater  and plans to renovate the theater are  moving forward it's been closed since  2004 in the past it's hosted  lots of bands the killers chili peppers  etc  local real estate developer jay dapper  bought the historic venue earlier this  year  and his plan is to renovate it into that  over the next  three years letting college athletes  make money coming up next we'll talk  about a new nevada law aimed at letting  university  athletes profit off their image and the  push to make that a national law as well  you're watching politics now  recently nevada lawmakers passed a bill  to allow college athletes to profit off  their image  their name and their likeness it kicks  in january 1st  proponents say it's a matter of fairness  and that it helps all athletes  the bill also includes a study on the  issue  nevada was the 17th state to pass that  law now  congress is considering passing similar  legislation federally  other laws for college athletes protect  their rights to  proper health care but as alexander  limon explains the hearing on  experiences of college athletes  also detailed abuses and injustices  college athletes came to capitol hill  thursday asking lawmakers to set uniform  standards for college athlete  compensation  college sports has become a  multi-billion dollar business that has a  financial monopoly  over its commodified athletes less than  two percent of ncaa athletes go on to  play professionally  meaning that the best years for them to  monetize their name image and likeness  is these four years  the ncaa says it's in the process of  changing its rules to allow athletes to  profit off  endo